# Enforce Unix-style line endings
* text=auto eol=lf

# Deny checkout of files with mixed line endings
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf

# Database migrations are checksummed by sqlx over their RAW BYTES, so a line
# ending is part of the identity of a migration. `-text` disables all
# translation: every clone on every OS gets the blob verbatim.
#
# Without this, a Windows working tree can hold CRLF copies of files git stores
# as LF (git normalises on `add` but never rewrites the working file), so a
# locally built engine and a CI-built engine compute different checksums for
# identical SQL. A database created by one is then rejected by the other with
# "migration N was previously applied but has been modified". That shipped once;
# see docs/agent-context/handoff.md.
*.sql -text

# Binary files
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
